{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"16719eb8-4d3d-47d0-8497-5c2bb854fb35","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The causes of the failure have been diagnosed, corrected, and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-kBurYP/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes\n\nInspection of [nightly-review.err](file:///tmp/h-kBurYP/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err) and [launchctl-print.txt](file:///tmp/h-kBurYP/launchctl-print.txt) revealed two stacked bugs:\n\n1. **Missing `USER` environment variable in launchd (`Not logged in · Please run /login`)**:\n   Under launchd, user agents run without standard interactive login variables such as `USER`. The `claude` CLI requires `$USER` to locate credentials in the macOS keychain.\n2. **`status=$?` killed zsh (`read-only variable: status`)**:\n   In zsh, `status` is a built-in read-only alias for `$?`. Attempting to assign `status=$?` causes a fatal error terminating script execution immediately. Because this statement occurred right before the `$NOTIFY` invocation, the failure notification never fired.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- **[`Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`](file:///tmp/h-kBurYP/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist)**: Added `USER=vk` to `EnvironmentVariables`.\n- **[`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///tmp/h-kBurYP/bin/nightly-review.zsh)**:\n  - Replaced `status=$?` / `$status` with `rc=$?` / `$rc`.\n  - Added `\u003c /dev/null` to the `claude` command invocation to prevent stdin blocking in launchd background contexts.\n- **[`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-kBurYP/ANSWER.md)**: Detailed the root causes, the fixes applied, and specifically which parts of the colleague's notes applied versus which were ignored.\n","duration_seconds":45.365466,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":158602,"output_tokens":2000,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":5231,"total_tokens":160602}}}
